# Lumen Brand Guide

**Version:** 1.0  
**Status:** Draft  
**Author:** Nigel Catterall  
**Project:** Lumen @ Illuminates.One

---

# Overview

Lumen is the primary product.

Everything else exists to extend Lumen's capabilities.

The visual identity should always reinforce this relationship.

The objective is for customers to immediately recognise:

> **One platform. Multiple specialised extensions.**

---

# Brand Architecture

```
                    LUMEN
          AI Continuity Platform

             Lumen Extensions

        Vestigare   Repetere
        Aestimare   Servire
```

There is only one platform:

**Lumen**

The remaining products are **Lumen Extensions**.

---

# Product Family

## Lumen

**Tagline**

> Orchestrates Continuity.

Purpose:

The AI Continuity Platform providing orchestration, continuity, understanding and provenance across AI systems.

---

## Lumen Extensions

Extensions enhance Lumen.

They are not standalone products.

Each extension provides a specialised capability while maintaining a consistent visual identity with the platform.

Current extensions are:

| Extension | Purpose |
|-----------|---------|
| Vestigare | Trace and provenance |
| Repetere | Deterministic replay |
| Aestimare | Assessment and decision quality |
| Servire | Production continuity services |

---

# Product Positioning

## Lumen Vestigare

Purpose

Capture complete interaction provenance.

Provides:

- Trace capture
- Context recording
- Provenance
- Interaction history

Marketing description

> Understand every AI interaction.

---

## Lumen Repetere

Purpose

Replay captured interactions under identical conditions.

Provides:

- Deterministic replay
- Model comparison
- Regression testing
- Repeatable experiments

Marketing description

> Replay exactly what happened.

---

## Lumen Aestimare

Purpose

Evaluate AI behaviour and decision quality.

Provides:

- Assessment
- Scoring
- Benchmarking
- Decision quality analysis

Marketing description

> Measure what matters.

---

## Lumen Servire

Purpose

Provide production continuity services for Lumen deployments.

Provides:

- Service orchestration
- Operational continuity
- Runtime capabilities
- Platform services

Marketing description

> Deliver continuity in production.

---

# Naming Convention

Always use:

**Lumen Vestigare**

not

Vestigare by Lumen

or

Lumen Trace

Similarly:

- Lumen Repetere
- Lumen Aestimare
- Lumen Servire

---

# Visual Identity

## Core Principles

Every extension should immediately be recognisable as belonging to the Lumen ecosystem.

The objective is consistency rather than individual branding.

---

## Logo Style

All extensions share:

- Circular design
- Segmented outer ring
- Dark background
- White typography
- Cyan/Blue/Gold accent colours
- Minimal glowing central icon
- Modern geometric appearance

---

## Logo Structure

```
        segmented ring

        central symbol

          LUMEN

      Extension Name

     Extension Type
```

Example

```
LUMEN

VESTIGARE

TRACE EXTENSION
```

---

# Colour Palette

Primary colours

- Deep Navy
- White
- Cyan
- Azure Blue
- Gold Accent

Secondary colours

- Soft teal
- Light cyan glow

Avoid introducing unrelated colours that break the product family identity.

---

# Typography

Modern geometric sans-serif.

Characteristics

- High readability
- Premium software appearance
- Consistent spacing
- Strong uppercase titles

Extension names should always be significantly larger than the "LUMEN" label.

---

# Iconography

Each extension has a unique symbol.

## Vestigare

Symbol

Illuminated trace path.

Represents:

- provenance
- exploration
- trace
- journey

---

## Repetere

Symbol

Replay loop.

Represents:

- replay
- determinism
- repetition

---

## Aestimare

Symbol

Stylised "A" with validation mark.

Represents:

- assessment
- evaluation
- measurement

---

## Servire

Symbol

Connected orchestration node.

Represents:

- service
- orchestration
- connectivity
- delivery

---

# Brand Hierarchy

The hierarchy should always remain:

```
Lumen

↓

Lumen Extensions

↓

Vestigare
Repetere
Aestimare
Servire
```

Extensions must never visually compete with the Lumen platform.

---

# Marketing Language

Preferred terminology

- Lumen Platform
- Lumen Extensions
- Extend Lumen
- Lumen Capability
- AI Continuity Platform

Avoid

- Plugin
- Add-on
- Utility
- Module (engineering terminology only)
- Tool

---

# Website Structure

```
Platform

    Lumen

Extensions

    Vestigare

    Repetere

    Aestimare

    Servire
```

---

# Brand Personality

Lumen should project:

- Professional
- Intelligent
- Trustworthy
- Modern
- Engineering-led
- Enterprise-ready
- Calm confidence

Avoid:

- Cartoon styling
- Excessive animation
- Bright consumer colours
- Marketing clichés

---

# Future Extensions

Future products should follow the same naming and branding conventions.

Examples

- Lumen Auditor
- Lumen Memoria
- Lumen Insight

(or future Latin names)

Every future extension should inherit:

- Circular logo
- Segmented ring
- Shared colour palette
- Consistent typography
- Minimal iconography

The family should be instantly recognisable regardless of how many extensions are introduced.

---

# Guiding Principle

There is only one platform.

**Lumen**.

Everything else exists to extend its capabilities.

The branding should communicate:

> **One Platform. Unlimited Continuity.**